{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For this time, etc.</b> He informed him of the severity of the plague according to the law of warning, which requires warning him concerning death itself — for if they warned him concerning a lighter death and come to execute him by a harsher one, he is exempt, as is known." "<b>All my plagues, etc.</b> It is difficult — did we not see that He brought upon him yet three other plagues afterward? And it would seem possible to say that this plague is weighted equally against all of them, corresponding to what they of blessed memory said (Rashi) that the plague of the firstborn is weighted equally against all the plagues. Or perhaps this one is weighted equally against all those preceding it, which are six plagues, and the plague of the firstborn is weighted equally against all those preceding it with the plague of hail included, and when you come to the count the plague of the firstborn is weighted equally against fourteen plagues — but this does not sit well with me." "And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that He intended to say to him: by the intensity of this plague his heart will be inclined to understand and to perceive the plagues that HaShem brought upon him. For it is to be understood that with each and every plague He brought until now, Pharaoh did not firmly conclude in his mind that they were from the God of omnipotence, but attributed them to sorcery and the deeds of demons — and this is the sign for you: even the sorcerers do likewise. And even though there was a plague regarding which the sorcerers said ״it is the finger of Elohim,״ there is room for Pharaoh to think that perhaps those men did not attain the level of Moses and Aaron in sorcery and therefore say so, and ultimately one will always find a sorcerer who can do likewise. Therefore HaShem said to him: <b>For this time</b>, by the intensity of the plague which I am about to bring upon you, I am sending all my plagues that I have already brought upon you <b>to your heart</b> — meaning, that you may know that they are not the deed of sorcery and demons but the deed of Elohim. And this is what He says — <b>my plagues</b> — with the appellation of the One who makes them, for when you see a wondrous plague which no demon or sorcery can perform even in approximate resemblance, such as bringing fire down from the heavens with wondrous marvels — then you will reflect upon the earlier ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :register {:flags {2 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:08.319206149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}